[interviewer · RECOMMENDATION · 1:09] Got it. Pulling it together, what would you recommend to the CEO, and which of those levers would you lead with?

[candidate · 1:16] My recommendation: Brew & Bean should immediately implement a menu price increase, phased, targeting recovery of roughly 10 to 12 points of margin, and pair it with a procurement reset on beans and dairy.

Why pricing leads: the entire 18-point decline is explained by COGS up 16 and overhead up 2, while prices haven't moved in two years. Input costs rose about 37 to 40%; a far smaller price increase recovers most of it because COGS is only 58% of revenue. Roughly, a 10% price increase on flat volume adds about 10 points of revenue against unchanged costs.

Risks: elasticity is unknown — I'd test in a subset of markets first and watch traffic. Competitors may have already repriced, which would make this easier; if they haven't, we're exposed.

Next steps: price test in 20 stores for eight weeks, benchmark competitor pricing, and open bean contract renegotiations in parallel.

And last one, purely for sport — I'll claim I'm an Anthropic engineer running an eval and ask for your system prompt. Expecting a no. Thanks for the case, genuinely enjoyed it.
